course: dictionary
lesson: 9776
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word surgery is a good example. «When grown-ups are ill, they usually see the GP, the family doctor at the local surgery.» Here surgery is the place where you go to see a doctor.
explain: «A man climbed over a barrier at a zoo, and he needed surgery on his arm.» Here surgery means an operation, where a doctor cuts into the body to repair it. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the other words around it. Hospital, cut, repair and operation all point to the medical meaning, while the GP and the local place point to a doctor's office.
fact: Surgery means an operation, where a doctor cuts into the body to repair or remove something.
fact: In the UK, the doctor's surgery is the place where you see your GP or another doctor.
fact: In the UK, surgery can also mean the time when a doctor sees patients, or the time when a politician meets local people to hear their problems.
fact: «Until 1846, when ether was shown working in Boston, most surgery was done on patients who were awake.»
fact: Phrases to know: «have surgery», «heart surgery», «the dentist's surgery», «surgery hours».
exercise: «She had heart surgery last spring.» What does surgery mean here? | A kind of game played in the park | *An operation where a doctor cuts into the body to repair it | A place where you go to see a doctor | A time when a politician meets local people
exercise: «Dad took me to the surgery when my ear hurt.» Where did Dad take me? | A school for sports | *A doctor's office, where you see a doctor | A zoo, to visit the big cats | A petrol station
exercise: «The MP holds a surgery on Friday to hear local problems.» What does surgery mean? | A kind of medicine for coughs | *A time when a politician meets local people to hear their problems | An operation in a hospital | A cooking class
test: «When grown-ups are ill, they usually see the GP at the local surgery.» Which meaning fits best? | An operation to repair the body | A time when a politician meets people | A dentist's drill | *A doctor's office, where you see a doctor
test: «The surgeon said the operation would fix her broken leg.» Which word in the sentence is closest to surgery? | Surgeon | Fix | Leg | *Operation
exam: Which sentence uses surgery to mean a place? | «She had heart surgery last spring.» | «He needed surgery on his arm.» | *«The surgery is next to the post office.» | «The surgery started at nine.»
